  "result": "Perfect! All 56 tests pass. I've added two new functions to manage invoice lines:\n\n**addLine(invoice, { sku, qty})** \u2014 Adds a line to a draft invoice:\n- If the SKU already exists, increases that line's qty by the given amount\n- If the SKU is new, adds it as a new line at the end\n- Validates qty (must be positive integer) and sku (must be in catalogue)\n- Returns `ok(newInvoice)` on success\n- Errors: `QTY_INVALID`, `UNKNOWN_SKU`, `NOT_DRAFT`\n\n**removeLine(invoice, sku)** \u2014 Removes a line from a draft invoice:\n- Returns `ok(newInvoice)` without that line\n- Errors: `NOT_DRAFT`, `LINE_NOT_FOUND`, `NO_LINES` (can't remove the last line)\n\nAdded two new error codes:\n- `NOT_DRAFT`: Can't modify an invoice that isn't in draft status\n- `LINE_NOT_FOUND`: The SKU doesn't exist on the invoice\n\nAdded 15 comprehensive tests covering:\n- Adding new lines and increasing existing ones\n- Removing lines (middle, last, non-existent)\n- All error conditions\n- Input immutability\n- Chaining operations together",
